          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            One proposal for a precise realization of the idea of “absolute”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1"} Spec(F1)
            is
            %em Borger’s absolute geometry
            (
            %a{:href => "#Borger09"}> Borger 09
            ). Here the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-ring"} Lambda-ring
            on a ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} spectrum
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R) \to Spec(\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+morphisms"} Frobenius morphisms
            and hence as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            data for descent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{F}_1)
            (which is defined thereby). This definition yields an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential geometric morphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+topos"} gros
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+toposes"} etale toposes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                  %mi Et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Et(Spec(\mathbb{Z}))
                  \\stackrel{\overset{}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{}{\longrightarrow}}}
                  Et(Spec(\mathbb{F}_1))
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right the notation is just suggestive, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            is a suitable one over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            which forgets the Lambda structure, and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+Witt+vectors"} ring of Witt vectors
            construction and may be thought of as producing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+jet+spaces"} arithmetic jet spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            here would be directly analogous to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            whose induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+comonad"} jet comonad
          %p
            This proposal seems to subsume many aspects of other existing proposals (see e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LeBruyn13"} Le Bruyn 13
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Et(Spec(\mathbb{F}_1))
            which is rich and genuinely interesting in its own right.
          %h2#Motivation Motivation
          %p
            The following is an attempt to motivate or make intuitively clear why lifts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+morphisms"} Frobenius morphisms
            may be related to “absolute geometry” over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1"} F1
          %p
            First of all, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            is analogous to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[z]
            over a finite field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{C}}
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entire+function"}> entire
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
          %p
            To make this analogy more concrete, notice that one characteristic property of the rings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[z]
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{C}}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\partial}{\partial z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            is recovered as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            generated by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideal"} maximal ideal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo −
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (z-x)
            there is the first order translation operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo −
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mfrac
                    %mo ∂
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo −
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{id} + (z-x)\frac{\partial}{\partial (z-x)}
            and the quotient by its difference from the identity is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/residue+field"} residue field
            of functions at the point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %p
            Therefore if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            is analogous to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[z]
            and to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{C}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideals"} maximal ideals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p)
            given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "-power" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^p : \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}
            (acting on the underlying set of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fermat%27s+little+theorem"} Fermat's little theorem
            is indeed of the above form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi n
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi n
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mi p
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                  %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (-)^p : n \mapsto n^p = n + p \cdot\partial_p n
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here the expression
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_p n \in \mathbb{Z}
            is uniquely defined by this equation, it is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fermat+quotient"} Fermat quotient
            operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi n
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≔
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi n
                        %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mi n
                    %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial_p : n \mapsto \partial_p n \coloneqq \frac{n^p - n}{p}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analogy
            it makes sense to think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_p : \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}
            as being like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
            – it is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-derivation"} p-derivation
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+differential+equations"} arithmetic differential equations
            (
            %a{:href => "#Buium05"}> Buium 05
            ).
          %p
            More generally, a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[z]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is to be thought of as a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(A)
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(k[z])
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            on the latter canonically lifts to the former, and is given by the same formula:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi z
                        %mo −
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{id} + (z-x)\frac{\partial}{\partial (z-x)}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(A) \to \mathrm{Spec}(k[z])
            is simply a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(A/(z)) \to \mathrm{Spec}(k)
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+line"} affine line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_k = \mathrm{Spec}(k[z])
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is to be thought of as a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(R)
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
            and the above arithmetic translation operator canonically lifts to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(R)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \mapsto a^p
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(R)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} supported
            over the point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{F}_p)
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+characteristic"} characteristic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            the
            = succeed "-power" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+homomorphism"} Frobenius homomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Frob
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Frob}_p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} formally dual
            morphisms for maps between rings that are not necessarily homomorphisms, then this situation is, possibly, usefully visualized as follows.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Frob
                                %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔽
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                              %mo +
                              %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔽
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                              %mo +
                              %mi p
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(R)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\mathrm{Frob}_p + 0}{\longrightarrow}
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(R)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{F}_p)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\mathrm{id} + 0}{\longrightarrow}
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{F}_p)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\mathrm{id} + p \cdot \partial_p}{\longrightarrow}
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
                  }
          %p
            This suggests that we are to think of the operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                  %mo +
                  %mi p
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^p = \mathrm{id} + p \cdot \partial_p
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
            not just as analogous to the identity transformation plus a derivation, but as analogous to the sum of a general finite transformation plus a derivation. In other words, a lift of this operation to some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(R)
            is to be a choice of ring homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi : R \to R
            (a “finite translation”) in addition to a derivation-like operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_p : R \to R
            (the “infinitesimal translation”), such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo +
                  %mi p
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (-)^p = \Phi + p \cdot\partial_p
                  \\,.
          %p
            As before, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is invertible in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{F}_p)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_p
            is uniquely fixed by this equation once
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            is chosen, and hence it is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            alone which is to be chosen on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,\Phi)
            satisfying the above equation is equivalently a “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_p
            \-ring” (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda+ring"} Lambda ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                  %mo +
                  %mi p
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{id} + p \cdot\partial_p
            for all primes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and hence are to ask that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            satisfies the above equation for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and hence defines for all primes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            the derivation-like operator (function on the underlying set of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi p
                    %mi Φ
                  %mo ≔
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mi Φ
                    %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial^\Phi_p  \coloneqq \frac{(-)^p - \Phi}{p} : R \to R
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the general form of an “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+jet+space"}> arithmetic differential operator
            ”, see for instance the first pages of (
            %a{:href => "#Buium13"}> Buium 13
            ) for review.
          %p In terms of the abuse of notation already employed previously, this situation is usefully visualized as follows.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi Φ
                              %mo +
                              %mi p
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msubsup
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi p
                                %mi Φ
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                              %mo +
                              %mi p
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(R)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\Phi + p\cdot \partial^{\Phi}_p}{\longrightarrow}
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(R)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\mathrm{id} + p\cdot \partial_p}{\longrightarrow}
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
                  }
          %p
            A ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            equipped with such an endomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda+ring"} Lambda ring
            (an insight highlighted by
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Borger"} James Borger
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the
            = succeed "-analog" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(R) \to \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z})
            as being like a product by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+line"} affine line
            over the non-existent field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
            of a map to “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{F}_1)
            ”. This should be one way to think of how
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_1
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Borger09"} Borger 09
          %p
            Finally notice that the refinement of the
            = succeed "-operation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+arithmetic+geometry"} E-infinity arithmetic geometry
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+operations"} power operations
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, remark 2.2.9
            )
          %h2#definition Definition
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of (finitely generated)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi Ring
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda Ring
            for that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %em
              %a{:href => "Lambda-ring#FreeAndCofreeLambdaRings"} here
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \;\colon\; \Lambda Ring \longrightarrow CRing
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            has
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Symm
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Symm
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+functions"} symmetric functions
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                given by forming the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+Witt+vectors"} ring of Witt vectors
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Symm
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Witt
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi Ring
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Witt
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Symm
                  %mi CRing
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (Symm \dashv U \dashv Witt)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\Lambda Ring
                  \\stackrel{\overset{Symm}{\leftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{U}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{Witt}{\leftarrow}}}
                  CRing
                  \\,.
          %p Hence
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings+of+Witt+vectors"} rings of Witt vectors
                are the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-free+functors"} co-free
                  Lambda-rings;
            %li
              %p
                rings of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+functions"} symmetric functions
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
                Lambda-rings.
          %p
            Regarding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring^{op}
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+categories"} opposite categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Witt
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Symm
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Symm
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Witt
                  %mi Λ
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (Witt \dashv U \dashv Symm)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  CRing^{op}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{Witt}{\longrightarrow}}{
                  \\stackrel{\overset{U}{\longleftarrow}}{
                  \\overset{Symm}{\longrightarrow}
                  }
                  }
                  \\Lambda Ring^{op}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi et
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{Z})_{et}
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
            equipped with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+topology"} etale topology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Et(Spec(\mathbb{Z}))
                  \\coloneqq
                  Sh(Spec(\mathbb{Z})_{et})
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+topos"} gros
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+topos"} etale topos
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
          %p
            Put a compatible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            on
            = succeed "(\u2026)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %msup
                      %mi Ring
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda Ring^{op}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi et
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{F}_1)_{et}
          %p In analogy we write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Et(Spec(\mathbb{F}_1))
                  \\coloneqq
                  Sh(Spec(\mathbb{F}_1)_{et})
          %p
            and speak of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+topos"} etale topos
            over
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{F}_1)
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
          %p
            The above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            on sites then induces a sequence of adjoint functors on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+presheaves"} categories of presheaves
            by left and right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Symm
                                %mo *
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi Symm
                                %mo *
                              %mo ≃
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Symm
                              %mo !
                            %mo ≃
                            %msup
                              %mi U
                              %mo *
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Witt
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mo !
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi Witt
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Witt
                          %mo !
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PSh(Spec(\mathbb{Z})_{et})
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{Witt_!}{\longrightarrow}}{
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{U_! \simeq Witt^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{Symm_! \simeq U^\ast \simeq Witt_\ast}{\longrightarrow}}{
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{Symm^\ast \simeq U_\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{
                  \\stackrel{Symm_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                  }
                  }
                  }
                  }
                  PSh(Spec(\mathbb{F}_1)_{et})
          %p The top three restrict to sheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Symm
                            %mo !
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi U
                            %mo *
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi Witt
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mo !
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi Witt
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Witt
                          %mo !
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh(Spec(\mathbb{Z})_{et})
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{Witt_!}{\longrightarrow}}{
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{U_! \simeq Witt^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{
                  \\stackrel{Symm_! \simeq U^\ast \simeq Witt_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                  }
                  }
                  Sh(Spec(\mathbb{F}_1)_{et})
          %p
            The induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo !
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Witt
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo !
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Witt
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (W^\ast \dashv W_\ast)
                  \\coloneqq
                  ( U_! \circ Witt_!  \dashv U_! \circ Witt_\ast)
                  \\,.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk+bundle"} infinitesimal disk bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊣
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+comonad"} jet comonad
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original article which proposes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
            as a realization of
            = succeed "-geometry" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1"} F1
          %ul
            %li#Borger09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Borger"}> James Borger
              ,
              %em Lambda-rings and the field with one element
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0906.3146"}> arXiv/0906.3146
              )
          %p This is based on technical details laid out in
          %ul
            %li#Borger08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Borger"}> James Borger
                ,
                %em The basic geometry of Witt vectors, I: The affine case
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0801.1691"}> arXiv:0801.1691
                )
            %li#Borger10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Borger"}> James Borger
                ,
                %em The basic geometry of Witt vectors, II: Spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1006.0092"}> arXiv:1006.0092
                )
          %p More discussion relating to this includes
          %ul
            %li#LeBruyn13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lieven+Le+Bruyn"}> Lieven Le Bruyn
              ,
              %em Absolute geometry and the Habiro topology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.6532"}> arXiv:1304.6532
              )
          %p
            Related discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+jet+spaces"} arithmetic jet spaces
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Buium05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandru+Buium"}> Alexandru Buium
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Arithmetic differential equations
            %li#Buium13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandru+Buium"}> Alexandru Buium
                ,
                %em Differential calculus with integers
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5194"}> arXiv:1308.5194
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.unm.edu/~buium/statupdated.pdf"} slighly differing pdf
          %p
            Related discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+operations"} power operations
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+arithmetic+geometry"} E-infinity arithmetic geometry
            is around remark 2.2.9 of
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rational+and+p-adic+Homotopy+Theory"} Rational and p-adic Homotopy Theory
          %p
            Further discussion of and speculation on an analogy between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+operations"} power operations
            and Borger’s absolute geometry is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Guillot"}> Pierre Guillot
                ,
                %em Adams operations in cohomotopy
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0612327"}> arXiv:0612327
                )
            %li#MoravaSanthanam
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jack+Morava"}> Jack Morava
                , Rakha Santhanam,
                %em Power operations and Absolute geometry
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.lemiller.net/media/slidesconf/AbsolutePower.pdf"}> pdf
                )
